[{:db/id "q-49570/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0bcc565b987d26bf192f936c7579b4dde886a" :answer/id #uuid "33c96734-2ad9-57d3-9e84-dda67bdd1b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49570/selection/8c1c0a411e1b442281e89399b762cc5a499f1269abe61925f5afbc7c90b541e8" :answer/id #uuid "bceaabf6-e2ac-5530-8e7e-d9e4bbdf8792" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49570/selection/6d0a1a4901a34a4edb5309c3fda22d32ba968fc5f911016e03c5a3c6d6ea76ad" :answer/id #uuid "09d323c2-25c2-56f4-9c20-a4714aafdd2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49570/selection/7abe227ff739c42d2d407bc6602cca2a056ef6a1629c3f32008d8d61236586e4" :answer/id #uuid "51ab496c-1758-5e87-a707-094b00822798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le \\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49570/selection/13c0004b165b449a6b2b540fed692935a9ee264ded801b56bc89875a2e311257" :answer/id #uuid "287aaa36-e215-586d-a825-dad38dff21cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49570/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "01b6d9c9-1b64-5900-88bc-2e07371eacba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49570/selection/6d0a1a4901a34a4edb5309c3fda22d32ba968fc5f911016e03c5a3c6d6ea76ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-49570/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0bcc565b987d26bf192f936c7579b4dde886a" "q-49570/selection/8c1c0a411e1b442281e89399b762cc5a499f1269abe61925f5afbc7c90b541e8" "q-49570/selection/6d0a1a4901a34a4edb5309c3fda22d32ba968fc5f911016e03c5a3c6d6ea76ad" "q-49570/selection/7abe227ff739c42d2d407bc6602cca2a056ef6a1629c3f32008d8d61236586e4" "q-49570/selection/13c0004b165b449a6b2b540fed692935a9ee264ded801b56bc89875a2e311257"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49570" :question/id #uuid "6fc238f8-0118-5614-b187-86df412902ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-49570" :question/problem "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{n+3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{x}^{n+3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{n}\\cdot {x}^{3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{x}{3})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Since $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{x}{3}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,0<x\\le 3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-49570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abad9fa9-b426-50aa-aaa7-d472ea974f98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123440/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715" :answer/id #uuid "a54e3eac-82c9-50e9-b900-7091b6f10844" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123440/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0bcc565b987d26bf192f936c7579b4dde886a" :answer/id #uuid "6f7272c3-8422-5e70-89de-e66a3cdf649d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123440/selection/eb974af25f7cad614022cdd558a4e8472f5e3e606b024c17f3db85b309d0ab74" :answer/id #uuid "6bbb98b3-d2b1-5ecc-9064-52e74bbabd65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123440/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" :answer/id #uuid "988b4525-731b-5e21-af0c-42a89c551fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123440/selection/97581072c1182da5c79cbff80bd36b90488fccc8ed2ed4248e600fd1829507df" :answer/id #uuid "7dec88e2-fde6-5491-b9b5-40b4e82e7217" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123440/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f97c4742-5003-532f-8984-a74f6aa82ab0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123440/selection/eb974af25f7cad614022cdd558a4e8472f5e3e606b024c17f3db85b309d0ab74" :answer-field/choices ["q-123440/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715" "q-123440/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0bcc565b987d26bf192f936c7579b4dde886a" "q-123440/selection/eb974af25f7cad614022cdd558a4e8472f5e3e606b024c17f3db85b309d0ab74" "q-123440/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" "q-123440/selection/97581072c1182da5c79cbff80bd36b90488fccc8ed2ed4248e600fd1829507df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123440" :question/id #uuid "10527239-7a53-5ae0-a820-1a3f5dbaefa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-123440" :question/problem "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{2n+1}}{{x}^{n}},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{x}^{2n+1}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {x}^{2n}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =x\\cdot {x}^{2n-n} \\\\  & =x\\cdot {x}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=x.$ Since $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for\n\n$$\n0<x\\le 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123440/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abad9fa9-b426-50aa-aaa7-d472ea974f98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123440"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141322/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" :answer/id #uuid "5355b126-9eaf-5fe4-bcb4-4a7af42ec1c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141322/selection/98ff92445dc92a3eb402958e5d5f65f0c86bfcc7d7b2c116ada1e99a96b1c47d" :answer/id #uuid "f3bfc97f-ed1d-5a66-bcbf-48c8af2ba6d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141322/selection/8f9d5e78c71265e01c3fb8d0d07a71e7cb16e44cf95a17717304ef60938a6591" :answer/id #uuid "236cae10-5a3d-597c-8842-341b21b83caf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141322/selection/97581072c1182da5c79cbff80bd36b90488fccc8ed2ed4248e600fd1829507df" :answer/id #uuid "a2ff5f20-313c-54b4-8770-1e6cf917a637" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141322/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0