ct that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\n0<x\\le 2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141322/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126485fb-1b7f-5602-bc8d-05908ac6f37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141329/selection/143e8067d99e10346ddd8e30f47607c441325e4495f95ed75f9f66e68cd73349" :answer/id #uuid "594f0477-ebf9-5099-b4d5-418bcafe7cdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141329/selection/18a82edba82532c9879ee81d6f976e6f127cf5c01b13c5bd24e7336124576623" :answer/id #uuid "40e4f90a-9ace-5ed4-88bb-55f4b5312c46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141329/selection/8f9d5e78c71265e01c3fb8d0d07a71e7cb16e44cf95a17717304ef60938a6591" :answer/id #uuid "1b08e602-9acf-5d4b-90b0-4002ca59c6d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141329/selection/98ff92445dc92a3eb402958e5d5f65f0c86bfcc7d7b2c116ada1e99a96b1c47d" :answer/id #uuid "18811060-62e7-54ba-bdb7-e6b7744025bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141329/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" :answer/id #uuid "58562ea8-2102-5505-a2f0-cbd978b2b96a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141329/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eebc974a-217c-52db-8f75-ad777668b61e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141329/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" :answer-field/choices ["q-141329/selection/143e8067d99e10346ddd8e30f47607c441325e4495f95ed75f9f66e68cd73349" "q-141329/selection/18a82edba82532c9879ee81d6f976e6f127cf5c01b13c5bd24e7336124576623" "q-141329/selection/8f9d5e78c71265e01c3fb8d0d07a71e7cb16e44cf95a17717304ef60938a6591" "q-141329/selection/98ff92445dc92a3eb402958e5d5f65f0c86bfcc7d7b2c116ada1e99a96b1c47d" "q-141329/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141329" :question/id #uuid "1a6ea49d-aab8-5fc3-8d1f-fbad3bc51925" :question/math-academy-id "q-141329" :question/problem "Consider the geometric sequence ${a}_{n}=2x{(\\frac{16}{{x}^{4}})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{16}{{x}^{4}}.$ \nSince ${x}^{4}$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{16}{{x}^{4}}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{4}\\ge 16.\n$$\n\nTaking into account the fact that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\nx\\ge 2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141329/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126485fb-1b7f-5602-bc8d-05908ac6f37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141329"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347770/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer/id #uuid "981b5ffa-a0d4-5990-a936-459652f1649b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347770/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7665fa5-9555-5d76-96b9-b1d9f4ac714a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347770/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-347770/field-1/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347770/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "8225eb13-4cd4-5e81-ba79-8ee1fc4bff50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347770/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d95d1ccd-88ba-51fb-ae00-5a93ba3739e9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347770/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-347770/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347770" :question/id #uuid "eaf84dc0-2718-5769-b160-3819e150d27e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347770" :question/problem "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{5}^{n+1}}{{x}^{n}},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ Find the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges.\n\n$x$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{5}^{n+1}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot {5}^{n}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{n}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =5{(\\frac{5}{x})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{5}{x}.$ Since $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{5}{x}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,x\\ge 5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-347770/field-1" "q-347770/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abad9fa9-b426-50aa-aaa7-d472ea974f98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
